Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extends Phase 5's lighter-form fallback per explicit follow-up feedback:
users should get a genuine choice between chat and a compact grouped-row
form, be able to set a remembered default, and never get redirected off
the page to use chat.

EnablePileOnModal now has two tabs instead of one form:
- Quick setup: the same 2 fields, redesigned as horizontal label+control
  rows instead of a stacked form.
- Ask Teammates: the real Teammates chat, embedded inline via
  TeammatesChat's own size="compact" mode — no redirect to
  /dashboard/teammates. Pre-seeded with a message naming the actual
  client so the user never has to explain who or what.

Whichever tab is actually used to finish enabling is remembered
(browser-local) and opens by default next time.

Real gap found and fixed to make the chat tab actually work, not just
look like it does: Teammates chat had no tool at all for "enable a
worker" — every existing tool was narrower (enroll a prospect, run a
piece standalone, etc.). Added enable_pile_on, backed by a new shared
function (enablePileOnForEngagement in lib/enable-pile-on.ts) that both
the chat tool and the Quick-setup tab's new enable-with-config route call
— one function behind both surfaces, so they can't produce different
results. Also threaded buyerName through Library's server page down to
the modal, so the chat pre-seed reads naturally instead of "this client."

